{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A good name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better than precious ointment; and the day of death than the day of one's birth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better to go to the house of mourning, than to go to the house of feasting: for that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the end of all men; and the living will lay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sorrow ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better than laughter: for by the sadness of the countenance the heart is made better.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heart of the wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the house of mirth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better to hear the rebuke of the wise, than for a man to hear the song of fools.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the laughter of the fool: this also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely oppression maketh a wise man mad; and a gift destroyeth the heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the end of a thing than its beginning: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the patient in spirit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " better than the proud in spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not hasty in thy spirit to be angry: for anger resteth in the bosom of fools.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say not thou, What is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the cause",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that the former days were better than these? for thou dost not inquire wisely concerning this.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good with an inheritance: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by it there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " profit to them that see the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a defense, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " money ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a defense: but the excellence of knowledge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom giveth life to them that have it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Consider the work of God: for who can make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " straight, which he hath made crooked?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the day of prosperity be joyful, but in the day of adversity consider: God also hath set the one over against the other, to the end that man should find nothing after him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have I seen in the days of my vanity: there is a just ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that perisheth in his righteousness, and there is a wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that prolongeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his life",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his wickedness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not righteous over much; neither make thyself over wise: why shouldst thou destroy thyself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not over much wicked, neither be thou foolish: why shouldst thou die before thy time?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good that thou shouldst take hold of this; yes, also from this withdraw not thy hand: for he that feareth God shall escape from them all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wisdom strengtheneth the wise more than ten mighty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " who are in the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a just man upon earth, that doeth good, and sinneth not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also take no heed to all words that are spoken; lest thou hear thy servant curse thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For often also thy own heart knoweth that thou thyself likewise hast cursed others.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All this have I proved by wisdom: I said, I will be wise; but it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which is far off, and exceedingly deep, who can find it out?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I applied my heart to know, and to search, and to seek out wisdom, and the reason ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and to know the wickedness of folly, even of foolishness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " madness:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I find more bitter than death the woman whose heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " snares and nets, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " her hands ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bands: whoever pleaseth God shall escape from her; but the sinner shall be taken by her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, this have I found, saith the preacher, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "counting",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one by one, to find out the account:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which yet my soul seeketh, but I find not: one man among a thousand have I found; but a woman among all those have I not found.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.7.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.7.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, this only have I found, that God hath made man upright; but they have sought out many inventions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
